	(lib_symbols)
	(text "BLOCK: test_debug\n\nSCOPE\n  System-level bring-up hardware that no single functional block owns.\n  SWD debug connector (PA13 SWDIO, PA14 SWCLK, PB3 SWO), the USART3 debug\n  console header (PD8 DBG_TX, PD9 DBG_RX), a consolidated rail probe header,\n  and any cross-block isolation link that sits between two blocks rather\n  than inside one. Per-block test points live in their own block sheets\n  (DEC-0007). Bring-up access is on populate-if-needed connectors.\n\nINTERFACES - the binding contract between blocks.\nReconciled against docs/FAFF-2-Electronics-Full.svg (block diagram) and\nhardware/cubemx/ARIA_SRB_FAFF_2_POC_CBs_1.ioc (MCU pin-map authority).\nNeed something not listed here? Raise it - do not invent it.\n  IN   all rails (probe header)\n  IN   SWDIO / SWCLK / SWO / nRESET <- mcu\n  IN   DBG_TX / DBG_RX <- mcu (USART3)\n  OUT  none (observation only)\n\nSTATUS: stub. No circuitry drawn yet - this sheet is reserved for the\nfollow-up block task that owns this file. Invoke /schematic-style before\nthe first edit, and delete this note once the block is drawn."
